#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198023 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198381 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65a25c72-9fa7-58fc-bf45-9cc2761696ea" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Division Problems as Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "41696b59-d81e-5c49-a967-141f67934aa1" :question/math-academy-id "e-12359" :question/problem "Find a fraction that's equivalent to $1 \\div (-7).$" :question/worked-solution "We have to divide a positive number $({\\color{blue}{1}})$ by a negative one $({\\color{red}{-7}}).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n![](images/b3/b3fdb7fe402f5e8ebfdf8502e8173faaaa11082ed9f618884cd1770e764ffaac.svg)\n\nTo write down the number that goes in the box, recall that \n\n$$\n1 \\div 7 = \\dfrac{1}{7}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{1}} \\div {\\color{red}{(-7)}} = {\\color{red}-\\dfrac{1}{7}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198024 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198382 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0fe851f3-482c-5426-87b2-32ec3c1b40f6" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Division Problems as Mixed Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "e40e5f9e-aab7-53ed-8850-bd855f2b97a3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12360" :question/problem "Find a fraction that's equivalent to $(-5) \\div (-3).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we are dividing a negative number $({\\color{red}-5})$ by another negative number $({\\color{red}-3}).$ So the result will be positive:\n\n![](images/cc/cce63c47aea469b99cccad529462e33e193ff094efb7d3535cf8ca095d8c23a9.svg)\n\nNow, to write down the fraction that goes in the box, recall that\n\n$$\n5 \\div 3 = 1 \\,\\textrm{R}\\, 2 = 1 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-5)} \\div {\\color{red}(-3)} = {\\color{blue} 1 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198025 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198383 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d17ce34f-7d65-5f44-a1c0-dfd3c2ea55f6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Fractions With Negative Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "a650b9e6-c97c-5471-af2d-76a5cfb0caff" :question/math-academy-id "e-12361" :question/problem "What is the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{14} = \\dfrac{-3}{\\bbox[1pt, border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A positive number can be obtained if we divide two numbers that are either both positive or both negative.\n\nSo, given a positive fraction, we have the following equivalent notations:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{14} = \\dfrac{-3}{-14}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we see that the numerator on the right-hand side is negative $({{\\color{red}-3}}).$ Therefore, the missing denominator must be $({{\\color{red}-14}}){:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{14} = \\dfrac{-3}{\\bbox[2pt, border: 1pt solid black]{\\color{red}-14}}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447633 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198381 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65a25c72-9fa7-58fc-bf45-9cc2761696ea" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Division Problems as Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4aae8a7b-bdee-5758-8e93-759f0bda588c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447511} {:answer/id #uuid "85101e4a-6ff9-5cb9-8adc-c7d24013943e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447547} {:answer/id #uuid "8f90316b-355b-56c2-af67-ddd7eec7f3d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447555} {:answer/id #uuid "a05fc29a-cb5c-51dc-99a4-b19179fa711b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447564} {:answer/id #uuid "e7856f71-45cc-5c76-9007-5e147e8387a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}