o write down the fraction that goes in the box, recall that\n\n$$\n13÷6=2\\,\\text{R}\\,1=2\\,\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n13÷(-6)=-2\\,\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198383 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d17ce34f-7d65-5f44-a1c0-dfd3c2ea55f6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Fractions With Negative Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "039893a2-8d49-57cf-9a55-7abd0aa06682" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447481} {:answer/id #uuid "27c12289-8437-5fd2-8869-b0733101ec66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447495} {:answer/id #uuid "63583326-3ba6-5959-9bd7-fb1397fd8dc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447529} {:answer/id #uuid "7103a6f8-e92a-569c-a90c-72f0bba5770d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "99" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447536} {:answer/id #uuid "db299c2f-d642-5a55-8c24-36bede6e2788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-99" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "039893a2-8d49-57cf-9a55-7abd0aa06682" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447481} :answer-field/id #uuid "12eb66b1-4795-56a1-9c50-34b9a599aa9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447601}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "93f4a5cf-cbff-5d1e-aa34-eea593763369" :question/math-academy-id "q-162125" :question/problem "What is the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n-\\frac{11}{9}=\\frac{\\bbox[1pt,border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}{9}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A negative number can be obtained if we divide two numbers, one of which is positive and the other negative.\n\nSo, given a negative fraction, we have the following equivalent notations:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{11}{9}=\\frac{-11}{9}=\\frac{11}{-9}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we see that the denominator on the right-hand side is positive $(9).$ Therefore, the missing numerator must be $(-11):$\n\n$$\n-\\frac{11}{9}=\\frac{-11}{9}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447643 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198383 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d17ce34f-7d65-5f44-a1c0-dfd3c2ea55f6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Fractions With Negative Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f23769d-b5ad-5205-89cb-9958dda99b99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447498} {:answer/id #uuid "7ccb728e-4727-5592-ac9b-86cd9fa28275" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447543} {:answer/id #uuid "96ec2c4b-030b-5c5b-ae1b-b0b4b6296512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447559} {:answer/id #uuid "e3e21289-23fb-54ae-bb18-5e96b65d30f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "76" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447589} {:answer/id #uuid "f1816314-7ca6-5019-9914-d9b3b3d5c63d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-76" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96ec2c4b-030b-5c5b-ae1b-b0b4b6296512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447559} :answer-field/id #uuid "546e0e0e-829c-5d2d-ad6b-2c1c933c4e6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447606}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ec1af280-a6fd-52ab-9d3d-511d96573c0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-162136" :question/problem "What is the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{19}=\\frac{\\bbox[1pt,border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}{-19}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A positive number can be obtained if we divide two numbers that are either both positive or both negative.\n\nSo, given a positive fraction, we have the following equivalent notations:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{19}=\\frac{-4}{-19}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we see that the denominator on the right-hand side is negative $(-19).$ Therefore, the missing numerator must be $(-4):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{19}=\\frac{-4}{-19}\n$$"}]}
